==English==
[[File:Martha last passenger pigeon 1912.jpg|thumb|{{w|Martha (passenger pigeon)|Martha}}, the last known living passenger pigeon (d. 1914)]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A bird of the [[extinct]] species ''[[Ectopistes migratorius]]'', formerly endemic to [[North America]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Sense of an endling|author=Helen Lewis|authorlink=Helen Lewis (journalist)|work=New Statesman|date=2012-06-27|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120711122539/http://www.newstatesman.com/sci-tech/sci-tech/2012/06/sense-endling|archivedate=2012-07-11|passage= Martha was a remnant of a species that had once dominated North America; it is estimated that there were as many as four billion – yes, billion – '''passenger pigeons''' when the Europeans arrived. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Jonathan Elmore|title=Fiction and the Sixth Mass Extinction|year=2020|publisher=Rowman & Littlefield|chapter=Life Finds A Way|isbn=978-1-7936-1920-4|passage=Revive & Restore, a branch of the Long Now Foundation, is currently attempting to de-extinct the '''passenger pigeon''' in a project called The Great Comeback.}}

